       <property name="styleSheet">
        <string notr="true">color: #a06000;</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>(requires client reload to take effect - only affects newly (re)loaded splats)</string>
       </property>
       <property name="wordWrap">
        <bool>true</bool>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="2" column="0">
      <widget class="QLabel" name="pixelScaleLimitLabel">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>How small (in screen pixels) a LoD tree node's projected size must be before traversal stops refining past it. Smaller = more aggressive refinement (more detail everywhere, more nodes drawn, slower). Larger = coarser (fewer nodes, faster, blockier). Takes effect on the next traversal - no reload needed. Default 1.0.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>Pixel scale limit</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="2" column="1">
      <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="pixelScaleLimitDoubleSpinBox">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>How small (in screen pixels) a LoD tree node's projected size must be before traversal stops refining past it. Smaller = more aggressive refinement (more detail everywhere, more nodes drawn, slower). Larger = coarser (fewer nodes, faster, blockier). Takes effect on the next traversal - no reload needed. Default 1.0.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="decimals">
        <number>2</number>
       </property>
       <property name="minimum">
        <double>0.100000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="maximum">
        <double>20.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="singleStep">
        <double>0.100000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="value">
        <double>1.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="3" column="0">
      <widget class="QLabel" name="maxSplatsBudgetLabel">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>Hard cap on how many LoD tree nodes traversal will ever select in one frame, across all splat objects combined - a safety valve against a pathologically large scene, not a quality dial. If hit, detail is capped below what the scene would otherwise show (flagged as &quot;!WARNING!&quot; in Diagnostics when it happens). Takes effect on the next traversal - no reload needed. Default 10,000,000.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>Max splats budget</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="3" column="1">
      <widget class="QSpinBox" name="maxSplatsBudgetSpinBox">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>Hard cap on how many LoD tree nodes traversal will ever select in one frame, across all splat objects combined - a safety valve against a pathologically large scene, not a quality dial. If hit, detail is capped below what the scene would otherwise show (flagged as &quot;!WARNING!&quot; in Diagnostics when it happens). Takes effect on the next traversal - no reload needed. Default 10,000,000.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="minimum">
        <number>1</number>
       </property>
       <property name="maximum">
        <number>200000000</number>
       </property>
       <property name="singleStep">
        <number>100000</number>
       </property>
       <property name="value">
        <number>10000000</number>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="4" column="0">
      <widget class="QLabel" name="resortMoveThresholdLabel">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>How far (in world-space metres) the camera must move since the last LoD traversal/depth-sort before another one is worth kicking off. Smaller = LoD/sort updates more eagerly as you move (more CPU work). Larger = updates less often (cheaper, but detail/depth-order visibly lags behind camera movement, especially near large objects). Takes effect immediately - no reload needed. Default 0.1.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>Resort move threshold (m)</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="4" column="1">
      <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="resortMoveThresholdDoubleSpinBox">
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>How far (in world-space metres) the camera must move since the last LoD traversal/depth-sort before another one is worth kicking off. Smaller = LoD/sort updates more eagerly as you move (more CPU work). Larger = updates less often (cheaper, but detail/depth-order visibly lags behind camera movement, especially near large objects). Takes effect immediately - no reload needed. Default 0.1.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="decimals">
        <number>2</number>
       </property>
       <property name="minimum">
        <double>0.010000000000000</double>
